{"id": "Dfgk0_mIHym", "title": "Video by feartalkies", "description": "At a king's feast, one guest pushed his rice away: \"This rice smells of corpses.\" Everyone laughed… then they found where it grew.\n\nLast tale's answer: Vikram said Shashi, the husband her father chose. She was given to Shashi openly, in a wedding before the sacred fire, with everyone watching. Manaswami wed her in secret, \"in an underhand way, like a thief\" in the king's words. The Indian tellings add the rule: a secret garland-wedding is a rite for fairies and celestial beings, but ordinary people marry by public rites. Betaal asked: \"But Manaswami married her first!\" Vikram: nobody knew of that marriage, so it cannot outweigh one the whole court saw. Even with Manaswami's child on the way (older tellings), it is born into a public, lawful marriage.\n\nVikram & Betaal: Three Fussy Brothers.\n\nThe parts we couldn't fit in the reel:\n• The father was Vishnusvamin of Vrikshaghata in Anga; the king was Prasenajit of Vitankapura.\n• The brothers did reach the sea and pick up the turtle. The eldest backed off: \"slippery with slime\". The others laughed: \"If you see our duty so clearly, why do you not see that your own is the same?\"\n• The feast had \"all six flavours\". The whole court smelled the rice and called it fragrant. Told about the field, the pleased king said: \"eat of some other dish.\"\n• The lady wore sandalwood, camphor and black aloes. The second brother held his nose: \"I am a dead man.\" The doubting king, by \"artfully framed questions\", learned she had lost her mother AND her nurse as a child, and was raised on goat's milk.\n• The bed had seven mattresses. The king's officers searched them one by one and found the hair under them all. The king spent the whole night wondering how it could press so deep.\n• The reward was 300,000 gold pieces. The book ends: they stayed in comfort \"forgetting all about the turtle\", though they had \"incurred sin by obstructing their father's sacrifice.\"\n\nSo, the fussiest brother: food, women, or bed? Comment your pick and send this to your fussiest friend. 👇\n\n#vikrambetaal #indianhorror #ghoststories #indianfolklore #horrorstories", "channel": "feartalkies", "uploader_id": "58803293522", "uploader": "Fear Talkies | Indian Horror", "timestamp": 1794204334, "like_count": 2516, "comment_count": 20, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1131648383131941a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 69.691, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPhwHt0mZ23123pV03YOnWXTPqKMvwIrm7YnDZi64pd83FsZoEgdlzI8b_aTR_DG3229VJGbzT5CFeSETwx-nXT3iEm5OTJj7tjAIE.mp4?_nc_cat=102&_nc_oc=AdrQ8svtbsgnPJXu7JMT14uVW4m-DrIxjlUJXsNAq7RevqUsT6Q_uaTjBPeWHoQHYqOnC9TqiaCwvjTip_2Beh6w&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=oUIkbT4UL_UQ7kNvwEmBLyn&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=IOD780ClwXaYCmaCZYinFQ&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQQ48dvrIK5w9AV9DvV2OfEuRtc9WySgy_XWznrld3e_iA&oe=6AF459CF", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 69.691, "resolution": "audio only", "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "format": "dash-1131648383131941a - audio only (DASH audio)"}, {"url": "https: